    "notes": {
        "8398d189-9157-4f22-b56c-2ab20b27d070": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 304,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThe queue **appmixer-e2e-publish** must exist on the broker of the connected account and be bound to the **amq.direct** exchange with routing key **appmixer-e2e-publish**. The components never declare queues or bindings. Create both in the RabbitMQ management UI (Queues → Add queue; then on the queue page Bindings → From exchange `amq.direct`, routing key `appmixer-e2e-publish`).\n\nThe message is sent with `expiration` 120000 ms, so a message left over from a failed run is gone before the next run. Don't run this flow twice within two minutes. Keep only one consumer on this queue."
        }
    }
